{# Inputs: schemas, entities, searches and modules. DuckDB has no roles, GRANT, REVOKE or row-level security,
   so this template emits no simulated privilege statements. It states the enforcement boundary in the
   deployment record and lists the consumer surfaces an authenticated serving application must expose.
   Read-only connections prevent writes; they do not hide base tables, runtime memory or PII. #}
-- Access boundary: DuckDB provides no native principals. Authorisation is an external obligation.
{% for e in entities if not e.runtime %}
-- Consumer surface: {{ e.view }}
{% endfor %}
{% for e in entities if e.runtime %}
-- Runtime scope (application-enforced, not exposed): {{ e.qualified }}
{% endfor %}
{% for s in searches %}
-- Consumer search macro: {{ qualified(containers.search,s.name) }}
{% endfor %}
{% if 'semantic' in modules %}
-- Discovery entry point: {{ qualified(containers.access,'data_product_manifest') }}
{% endif %}
